WEBVTT

00:09:27.563 --> 00:09:30.107
We really need to figure out
better solutions.

00:09:30.774 --> 00:09:33.235
Sometimes, we can carve out
small exceptions

00:09:33.277 --> 00:09:35.029
to the confrontation clause,

00:09:35.029 --> 00:09:38.449
based on public policy
and the necessities of the case.

00:09:39.325 --> 00:09:41.827
Sometimes, remote testimony
can be a substitute

00:09:41.869 --> 00:09:44.038
for in-person presence,

00:09:44.079 --> 00:09:46.790
particularly if we build in
due process safeguards,

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:49.293
like having a person
from each side present,

00:09:49.293 --> 00:09:52.671
to make sure there isn't any
prompting or interference.

00:09:53.213 --> 00:09:54.840
During the pandemic,

00:09:54.840 --> 00:09:57.885
judges have sometimes permitted
remote testimony

00:09:57.926 --> 00:09:59.970
based on the public health crisis

00:09:59.970 --> 00:10:03.432
and the elevated risks
that that presents to seniors.